# Response headers for the published docs site.
#
# docs.<base-domain> is served by Cloudflare Pages (the erun-docs deploy Job
# uploads the Docusaurus build with wrangler), not routed through the cluster
# edge, so the edge's Strict-Transport-Security never reaches it. Pages reads
# this file from the deployed root and applies the headers to every response,
# including the custom domain's.
#
# max-age is one day, matching the edge's own value. HSTS cannot be recalled
# early -- a browser that has read the header refuses plaintext for that host
# until it expires -- so the short value keeps a TLS mistake recoverable while
# the commitment is proven. Raise it towards 31536000 (one year) only once
# every host under the domain is verified https-only; includeSubDomains is the
# step after that, not the first, because it binds names this site does not
# serve.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
